course: dictionary
lesson: 13049
title: Fastenings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A fastening is a thing that closes or joins two things together. Buttons, zips, buckles and Velcro are all fastenings. «Mia did up the buckle on her bag.» Here the buckle is the fastening that keeps the bag shut.
explain: Fasten is the verb, the action of closing something. Fastening is the noun, the thing that does the closing. You can count fastenings: one fastening, two fastenings. «The fastening on his coat was a broken zip.»
explain: The word can also mean the act of fixing or closing something. «Check the fastening before you climb the rope.» Here it means making the rope secure. Look at the words around it to see which meaning fits.
fact: A fastening is a thing used to close or join something.
fact: Buttons, zips, buckles, poppers, clips and Velcro are all fastenings.
fact: «Fastening» can also mean the act of closing or fixing something.
fact: Fasten is the verb: you fasten a seat belt, and the buckle is the fastening.
fact: Designers choose fastenings for bags and clothes, so they must be strong and easy to use.
exercise: «The fastening on his coat was a broken zip.» What is a fastening? | *A thing used to close or join something | A place where you buy clothes | A sound a door makes | A kind of cloth
exercise: Which of these is a fastening? | *Popper | Sock | Pencil | Puddle
exercise: «Please fasten your seat belt before we take off.» Find and copy the word that is a verb meaning close something. | seat | before | *fasten | take
test: «Designers chose strong fastenings for the school bag.» What does fastenings mean here? | *Things that close or join the bag | The colours of the bag | The weight of the bag | The shops where the bag is sold
test: «Bethan did up the fastening on her coat before going out into the rain.» What does did up mean? | Took off | *Fastened, closed | Washed | Painted
exam: «The bag had a strong fastening, so nothing fell out.» Why did nothing fall out? | Because the bag was empty | Because it was raining | Because the fastening held it closed | *Because the bag was too small
